From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:39:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/tablet-seat: Add a tablet when its first tool comes
 near

ClutterSeat::device-added is emitted when the stage processes its queued
events, on the next frame, while the Wayland seat sees every input event
as it arrives, from the display's event filter. Until then, events of a
new tablet don't count as tablet events and go nowhere. A tool that comes
into proximity right after its tablet appears, as a pen held near the
screen when a tablet is plugged in or the system resumes, never gets a
current tablet, and its proximity-out, which arrives once the tablet is
known, crashes in meta_wayland_tablet_update_sprite().

Route every event of a device with tablet tools to the tablet seat, add
the tablet when one of its tools enters proximity, and let the later
device-added signal find it already there. The tablet seat lets the
device-added event through, as it does device-removed, so the stage still
emits the signal for a tablet it already knows.
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-seat.c        | 5 +----
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-tablet-seat.c | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-seat.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-seat.c
index 7b7dff8..12ae900 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-seat.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-seat.c
@@ -420,10 +420,7 @@ is_tablet_event (MetaWaylandSeat    *seat,
   capabilities = clutter_input_device_get_capabilities (device);
 
   if (capabilities & CLUTTER_INPUT_CAPABILITY_TABLET_TOOL)
-    {
-      return meta_wayland_tablet_seat_lookup_tablet (seat->tablet_seat,
-                                                     device) != NULL;
-    }
+    return TRUE;
   if (capabilities & CLUTTER_INPUT_CAPABILITY_TABLET_PAD)
     {
       return meta_wayland_tablet_seat_lookup_pad (seat->tablet_seat,
diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-tablet-seat.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-tablet-seat.c
index 6464e87..98dd214 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-tablet-seat.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-tablet-seat.c
@@ -188,6 +188,10 @@ meta_wayland_tablet_seat_device_added (MetaWaylandTabletSeat *tablet_seat,
 {
   MetaWaylandSurface *pad_focus;
 
+  if (g_hash_table_contains (tablet_seat->tablets, device) ||
+      g_hash_table_contains (tablet_seat->pads, device))
+    return;
+
   pad_focus = meta_wayland_seat_get_input_focus (tablet_seat->seat);
 
   if (is_tablet_device (device))
@@ -378,6 +382,8 @@ meta_wayland_tablet_seat_update (MetaWaylandTabletSeat *tablet_seat,
   switch (clutter_event_type (event))
     {
     case CLUTTER_PROXIMITY_IN:
+      meta_wayland_tablet_seat_device_added (tablet_seat, device);
+      G_GNUC_FALLTHROUGH;
     case CLUTTER_PROXIMITY_OUT:
     case CLUTTER_BUTTON_PRESS:
     case CLUTTER_BUTTON_RELEASE:
@@ -442,6 +448,7 @@ meta_wayland_tablet_seat_handle_event (MetaWaylandTabletSeat *tablet_seat,
         return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
 
       return meta_wayland_tablet_pad_handle_event (pad, event);
+    case CLUTTER_DEVICE_ADDED:
     case CLUTTER_DEVICE_REMOVED:
       return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
     default:
